GPRIM byte-semantics handlers: byte-cast the cast-less _gprim sites (asm-audited per handler)

The 13 recovered poly handlers mix TWO Ghidra pointer semantics for _gprim1/_gprim2:
sites Ghidra emitted WITH an explicit (int) cast are byte offsets (correct as-is), and
cast-less pointer arithmetic is byte-based in SIX handlers (0x417f00/41867c/41bd3c/
41bd98/41c514/41c570 — asm stores at [reg+4]/[reg+7] and advances +0x10/+0x18 BYTES)
but element-based (int*) in the other seven (e.g. 0x41da48: `_gprim1 + 3` = +0xc bytes,
asm-verified). The reverted blanket patch 400 broke the element handlers; this patch
fixes ONLY the six byte-semantics handlers' cast-less sites (field stores at +4/+7 and
the record advances), each verified against the disassembly store table.

